    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0450" n="346" xml:id="pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4210: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-15T21:00:00+01:00">February 15, 1932—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 15—4:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. A meeting of the Twelve will be held tomorrow morning to discuss a
                    declaration proposed by the Secretary General which is called an appeal to Japan
                    but which is more vigorous in tone than this appellation would indicate.<anchor
                        n="48" xml:id="d365-f1"/></p>
                <p>After this discussion the Twelve will, if time permits, decide on China’s demand
                    for the summoning of the Assembly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d365-f1" n="48" xml:id="d365-f1-content">
                <p>With reference to this paragraph, the Secretary of State replied in telegram No.
                    15, February 15, 7 p.m., “This information is noted here with
                    gratification.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
